    "55bd100e-3bbd-426c-a5cf-eed7b2a3706f": {
      "type": "testimonials",
      "blocks": {
        "column_zJ6zMR": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "So much easier than brushing",
            "text": "<p>I've really tried to brush my spaniel's teeth for several years but she gets so stressed every time. With these it goes so much smoother, she doesn't seem to mind as much. Takes maybe a minute in the evening and the wipe gets dirty afterwards which gives me hope that it works. Her breath has gotten a bit better too, not as bad as before when she comes to give kisses.</p>",
            "author": "Jennifer M, 58 - 2025-11-12"
          }
        },
        "column_qUghpJ": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Vet said do something - this works",
            "text": "<p>Talked to my vet about dental care and she said the most important thing is to do SOMETHING regularly, even if you can't brush. These wipes have made it so much easier for me to keep the routine. My 11-year-old dachshund has noticeably whiter teeth and I feel safe using the natural ingredients. Takes barely a minute a day. Highly recommend!</p>",
            "author": "Anne B, 57 - 2025-11-09"
          }
        },
        "column_FGVAjz": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Finally something that actually works",
            "text": "<p>Really good. I've tried chew toys, water additives, everything possible. Nothing worked and my dog's breath was TERRIBLE. These wipes actually remove the dirt, you see it directly on the wipe. Takes max 2 minutes and I can do it while watching TV. Should've bought these ages ago.</p>",
            "author": "Sophie H, 43 - 2025-10-28"
          }
        },
        "column_8RKF7m": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Safe for the whole family",
            "text": "<p>We have a 3-year-old at home and the dog licks him constantly. I wanted something for the dog's breath that isn't dangerous if the kids get it on them. These are natural and work really well. Takes 2 minutes in the evening when the kids are asleep. The dog sits calmly and his breath is so much fresher now. Great not to have to worry when he kisses the kids!</p>",
            "author": "Sarah E, 39 - 2025-10-03"
          }
        },
        "column_ya4rpx": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Getting better each time",
            "text": "<p>My dog wasn't fond of it at first. But now it's going better. It works.</p>",
            "author": "Christine B - 2025-09-21"
          }
        },
        "column_R3wwEK": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Worth every penny",
            "text": "<p>I can actually get through with my dog's dental care now 😊 Worth every penny.</p>",
            "author": "Emily R, 41 - 2025-09-15"
          }
        },
        "column_gCBCNY": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Works really well on bad breath",
            "text": "<p>My French bulldog had terrible breath that was hard to deal with as well as her dog's teeth. Works really well!</p>",
            "author": "Jessica T, 36 - 2025-09-15"
          }
        },
        "column_89igQU": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Teeth much whiter now",
            "text": "<p>My puppy is 9 years old and has always been difficult to get to cooperate like he should. The teeth look much whiter after a couple of weeks. Recommend!</p>",
            "author": "Susan M, 47 - 2025-09-02"
          }
        },
        "column_8ANdnq": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Our new evening routine",
            "text": "<p>Every evening after the last walk we put on a 'finger sock' on our teeth. It has become my and my dog's routine for both of us. The teeth look a bit cleaner now after a few weeks. Feel good about doing something instead for not doing anything at all like the vet said.</p>",
            "author": "Karen A, 61 - 2025-08-29"
          }
        },
        "template--21507361800487__55bd100e-3bbd-426c-a5cf-eed7b2a3706f-column-1": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "Highly recommended!!",
            "text": "<p>My dog has always been afraid of toothbrushing, which made it difficult to keep his teeth clean.<br/><br/>But after we started using these wipes, he’s become completely calm.<br/><br/>It’s amazing to see that he no longer runs away or gets anxious when it’s time to clean his teeth.</p>",
